<section class="model-architecture" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
  <p class="section-label">Architecture</p>
  <div>
    <h2 id="architecture-title">How activity travels through the circuit</h2>
    <p class="architecture-copy">
      The prefrontal cortex (PFC) provides input to both CA3 and CA1. In this simplified model,
      the mossy fiber-like input reaches CA3 directly, bypassing the dentate gyrus (DG), while
      the temporoammonic pathway carries input to CA1. CA3 also projects to CA1 through
      Schaffer collaterals. Cortical input influences when ripples occur across slow oscillation states.
    </p>
    <p class="architecture-copy">
      Within CA3, recurrent excitation between pyramidal neurons generates large population events
      that propagate to CA1. Within CA1, recurrent inhibitory circuitry helps synchronize this activity
      to produce SPW-Rs. The small circuits below illustrate these two dominant motifs.
    </p>
    <figure class="architecture-panel">
      <svg class="region-diagram" viewBox="0 0 560 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="region-diagram-title region-diagram-desc">
        <title id="region-diagram-title">PFC input to CA3 and CA1, with a CA3 projection to CA1</title>
        <desc id="region-diagram-desc">PFC projects directly to CA3 through a mossy fiber-like model pathway that bypasses DG, and to CA1 through the temporoammonic pathway. Schaffer collaterals carry activity from CA3 to CA1.</desc>
        <defs>
          <marker id="architecture-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" class="arrowhead" />
          </marker>
        </defs>
        <path class="connection" d="M 256 77 L 123 213" marker-end="url(#architecture-arrow)" />
        <path class="connection" d="M 304 77 L 437 213" marker-end="url(#architecture-arrow)" />
        <path class="connection" d="M 136 240 L 424 240" marker-end="url(#architecture-arrow)" />
        <circle class="region" cx="280" cy="52" r="34" />
        <circle class="region" cx="100" cy="240" r="34" />
        <circle class="region" cx="460" cy="240" r="34" />
        <text class="region-name" x="280" y="58">PFC</text>
        <text class="region-name" x="100" y="246">CA3</text>
        <text class="region-name" x="460" y="246">CA1</text>
        <text x="96" y="116">Mossy fiber-like input</text>
        <text class="diagram-note" x="96" y="138">DG bypassed in the model</text>
        <text x="456" y="116">Temporoammonic</text>
        <text x="456" y="138">pathway</text>
        <text x="280" y="222">Schaffer collaterals</text>
      </svg>
      <div class="local-circuits">
        <div class="local-circuit">
          <h3>CA3 · recurrent excitation</h3>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 260 140" role="img" aria-labelledby="ca3-circuit-title">
            <title id="ca3-circuit-title">Three pyramidal neurons linked by recurrent excitatory connections</title>
            <defs>
              <marker id="ca3-excitatory-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" class="arrowhead" />
              </marker>
            </defs>
            <path class="connection" d="M 112 39 L 70 88" marker-start="url(#ca3-excitatory-arrow)" marker-end="url(#ca3-excitatory-arrow)" />
            <path class="connection" d="M 81 111 L 179 111" marker-start="url(#ca3-excitatory-arrow)" marker-end="url(#ca3-excitatory-arrow)" />
            <path class="connection" d="M 190 88 L 148 39" marker-start="url(#ca3-excitatory-arrow)" marker-end="url(#ca3-excitatory-arrow)" />
            <circle class="pyramidal" cx="130" cy="27" r="19" />
            <circle class="pyramidal" cx="60" cy="111" r="19" />
            <circle class="pyramidal" cx="200" cy="111" r="19" />
            <text class="cell-letter" x="130" y="32">P</text>
            <text class="cell-letter" x="60" y="116">P</text>
            <text class="cell-letter" x="200" y="116">P</text>
          </svg>
          <p>Pyramidal cells excite one another, amplifying and sustaining population activity.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="local-circuit">
          <h3>CA1 · recurrent inhibition</h3>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 260 140" role="img" aria-labelledby="ca1-circuit-title">
            <title id="ca1-circuit-title">Two pyramidal neurons recruit a PV interneuron that feeds inhibition back to the pyramidal cells</title>
            <defs>
              <marker id="ca1-excitatory-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" class="arrowhead" />
              </marker>
              <marker id="ca1-inhibitory-bar" viewBox="0 0 10 12" refX="5" refY="6" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="7" orient="auto">
                <path d="M 5 1 L 5 11" class="inhibitory-bar" />
              </marker>
            </defs>
            <path class="connection" d="M 71 93 L 111 45" marker-end="url(#ca1-excitatory-arrow)" />
            <path class="connection" d="M 189 93 L 149 45" marker-end="url(#ca1-excitatory-arrow)" />
            <path class="connection inhibitory" d="M 111 22 Q 37 15 52 86" marker-end="url(#ca1-inhibitory-bar)" />
            <path class="connection inhibitory" d="M 149 22 Q 223 15 208 86" marker-end="url(#ca1-inhibitory-bar)" />
            <circle class="interneuron" cx="130" cy="27" r="19" />
            <circle class="pyramidal" cx="60" cy="111" r="19" />
            <circle class="pyramidal" cx="200" cy="111" r="19" />
            <text class="cell-letter interneuron-letter" x="130" y="32">I</text>
            <text class="cell-letter" x="60" y="116">P</text>
            <text class="cell-letter" x="200" y="116">P</text>
          </svg>
          <p>Pyramidal cells recruit PV interneurons, which feed inhibition back to coordinate firing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <span><i class="key-pyramidal"></i>P · pyramidal cell</span>
        <span><i class="key-interneuron"></i>I · PV interneuron</span>
        <span>→ Excitation</span>
        <span>⊣ Inhibition</span>
        <span class="schematic-note">Simplified circuit motifs; not all connections are shown.</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

